cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "less_slow.cpp: Less Slow Coding Practices in C++ 20, C, CUDA, PTX, & Assembly, from Numerics & SIMD to Coroutines, Ranges, Exception Handling, Networking, & User-Space IO"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.11.1
repository-code: https://github.com/ashvardanian/less_slow.cpp
url: https://ashvardanian.com/tags/less-slow/
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21612057
abstract: >-
  Educational micro-benchmarks for building a performance-first mindset in
  C++20, C, CUDA, PTX, and Assembly, measuring the real cost of abstractions
  from a few nanoseconds upward. It spans numerics and approximate math,
  SIMD kernels for AVX-2, AVX-512, and AMX on x86 alongside NEON, SVE, and
  SVE2 on Arm, branch prediction and pipeline effects, memory allocators and
  cache-friendly data layouts, coroutines, ranges, senders, and executors,
  string splitting, regular expressions, and JSON parsing, trees, graphs, and
  structure packing, plus user-space networking with io_uring and ASIO. On
  GPUs it covers Tensor Core generations from Volta SM70 and Ampere SM80
  through Hopper SM90a, including hand-written PTX, WGMMA, and DPX kernels
  for dynamic-programming workloads.

